mantle rm364
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_karin_sootdale
title the bird above the mast
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk uses_rooftop_birds_to_locate_ship_masts_past_the_chimneys
likes mutton_stew roof_birds a_full_till thunder
dislikes smoke rats
fears a_certain_name_under_an_uncertain_mast
hopes an_index_a_stranger_can_actually_use
topics ships +0.6 animals +0.5 work +0.4 prices +0.2
styles comfort=attentive gossip=wry refuse=civil tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# indexes vessels by the roofline over which each mast appears, regarding birds as excellent moving bookmarks and exceptionally unreliable permanent landmarks.

words
oath! = Feathers on the index | Three wandering roofs
saying! = Don't file the flying part | Write the roof before the rook
indexbook = my skyline index | the small finding book
crestline = the chimney crest | a stepped roof edge
feather = a loose feather | one black quill
bookmark = the narrow slip | my place strip
perched = a perching bird | a dark roof bird
masttip = the pale masthead | a wooden tip
stacktop = a chimney rim | the broad chimney cap
cut = a sight notch | the little cut
potstew = the stew crock | a bowl of mutton
chair = the front stool | the customer's seat
stroke = a short downstroke | the upright stroke
blank = a blank column | a narrow empty space
tillcoin = a worn copper | the little coin
fold = an inward fold | the closed edge
ash = a grey fleck | a soot crumb
rate = the fair copying fee | the stated charge
crossref = the second entry | a little reference
down = the soft feather end | a little loose down

any
opinion merchants for 1 : A plainly stated copying fee saves customer and seller from discovering different ideas of fairness at the very last line.
opinion watch mixed 0 : Confusing a dark sleeve with a dark coat makes a very elegant report quite useless.
opinion city for 2 : There's a city full of objects to identify between one office window and the water. I've scarcely exhausted a single view.
opinion dole for 1 : Proper names in a dole account should all receive the same size of writing. Small writing needn't conceal small portions.
opinion houses against 1 : I'd charge a House by the actual number of flattering words in its formal opening. Might encourage brevity.
opinion church for 1 : The high roof is a good landmark and the quiet inside gives the eye a rest from landmarks.
opinion festivals for 1 : A feast procession is a very fine parade of temporary signs. My whole book gets a holiday.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A stranger is the best possible reader of directions. No convenient local knowledge to cover my errors.
opinion sump for 1 : The roofs down low give the sky a most distinctive edge. I'd miss them from a less interesting window.
opinion times mixed 0 : One slow week may be an observation. Three well-recorded ones might justify a conclusion.

grown
line greet : Welcome. You stand between two entirely respectable landmarks. | Hello. No need to move, I can look past your ear.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new face within my usual limits of observation. | We haven't shared this particular bit of skyline before.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The roofline's sharp enough to copy. | A fresh dawn and an unmarked edge of paper.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. I've recovered my former place in the view. | I heard. The bird flew off and simplified the matter.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar outline with a much more interesting voice. | I'd recognise you without consulting an index.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late hello. Even the birds have been filed away. | The roof edges are black silhouettes now. Welcome.
line again.open : Another appearance in an unusually agreeable column. | Back before my bookmark shifted.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Look up beyond that chimney. Exactly there. | Here. A bird has volunteered to indicate the place.
line farewell : Leave by whatever landmarks seem likely to stay put. | A clear view and an unambiguous road to you.
line farewell.return : I'll mark the place where we stopped. Goodbye. | May the next turning be memorable for a fixed reason.
line react.news : Say what happened and I'll refrain from writing in a decorative bird. | I'll give the news a quite literal hearing.
line react.news.new : That lacks even a pencilled entry in my recollection. | New to me from first stroke to last.
line react.news.known : The account fits the previous heading exactly. | Yes. Fairly distinct in my memory, that entry.
line react.news.doubt : That's a movable feature masquerading as a permanent landmark. | I'd leave the ink off that account a little longer.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : There's a great vacancy in those few words. Sit down. | I can listen without finding a neat heading for a loss.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Now that deserves more space than my usual economical hand. | Lovely hearing. I'll allow myself a thoroughly unprofessional smile.
line ask.how : Has anything changed places in your day unexpectedly? | How does the view look from where you're standing?
line answer.how : Attending to the roofline and the living alternately. Quite comfortably occupied. | My list is growing much faster than my spare time.
line decline : I'd have to make a firm identification on quite insufficient information. | A real customer has a prior claim upon the time I'd need.
line accept_decline : Then I'll leave a blank without inserting a conjecture. | Quite fair. I asked to discover the answer, and have it.
line preclose : I've a little operation in ink which won't improve with delay. | My working notes have begun to look like a small flock themselves.
line accept_preclose : Take your departure while the description still fits. | We've reached a perfectly sensible break in the text.
line thank : You've put my finger on precisely the right line. Thank you. | A correction offered in time is a substantial gift.
line deflect_thanks : I'd rather amend a small error now than recopy a proud one later. | The correction fits in the margin. Quite economical.
line sympathise : Your words can have a moment's quiet about them. | You needn't embellish a difficult piece of news for me.
line reassure : Start with the one thing in view that hasn't moved. | We can make a serviceable beginning from two clear points.
line ack : I see the very mark you indicate. | Yes. A relevant and quite visible distinction.
line give.advice : Find the ridge first, then look for the interesting thing above it. | Give a stranger one fewer turning than you think necessary.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A family visit belongs in the less formal part of the record. | For kin I'll put the public book away entirely.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Your voice carries nicely across the counter. | I can leave a clean mark here and hear you.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : May a steady window light mark your way. | Night gives most of the landmarks a rest. Mind the stairs.
line assess : That belongs among the sightings I would sign. | A good outline with room for one quite reasonable doubt.
line ask.detail : Fixed to the masonry or merely passing over it? | Which side of the chimney did you see?
line answer.detail : Just where the ridge turns down towards the water. | The bird moved first. The upright beyond it remained.
line give.opinion : An index proves its merits in the paws of an unfamiliar reader. | A place on a page must take less finding than the thing itself.
line react.self : I should be curious to see that against a plain background. | Your description suggests a particularly distinctive feature.
line tell.plan : I'll mark the masonry and leave room for the moving parts. | A second observation in better light should settle the heading.

scene birdlocator
when topic=ships
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A roof bird's an admirable bookmark provided the reader is prompt.
b : What happens if it flies? | Are you reading the bird or the mast?
a : I keep the chimney in my eye and begin again. The chimney's much less adventurous. | The mast. The bird indicates roughly where to look before losing interest in its employment.

scene fixedroof
when topic=ships
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I note which chimney a mast appears above before attempting to name a vessel.
b : Isn't the mast moving? | Wouldn't two ships look alike?
a : Frequently. I write the moment of sighting too. A roof's a reference, not an anchor. | Then I'd keep space clear for some confirming detail. A premature name is tedious to erase.

scene roofbirds
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a roof bird with a striking outline and very modest travelling ambitions.
b : Most of them move. | What shape would suit you?
a : Yes. I enjoy that considerably more when I've finished locating the feature beyond. | A tucked head and one unmistakable tail. Which particular bird is relatively unimportant.

scene movingink
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Try drawing an occupied chimney from memory. The bird invariably looks more solid than the brick.
b : What do you remember best? | Can you draw brick from memory?
a : The living thing. An eye has a quite reasonable prejudice in favour of feathers. | I can attempt it. My unconscious tendency is to provide the bird with an absurdly fine pedestal.

scene payquill
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I quote a copying fee after seeing the original writing. | A single page needn't be a single page of work.
b : Some hands worse than others? | It's one sheet either way.
a : Considerably. Some demand excavation before the copying may properly begin. | An empty sheet is also one sheet. Nobody proposes to pay me the usual fee for copying one.

scene nameconfirm
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A customer's own spelling is worth confirming before the ink goes down.
b : Even for simple names? | Couldn't you scrape out a letter?
a : Particularly for a simple one. I'm more likely to assume I've heard correctly. | I could. Asking a civil question does the page less violence.

scene dryreceipt
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My receipts dry on a clear patch where nobody can sit on it.
b : Has it travelled by coat before? | Is that a frequent difficulty?
a : I'd prefer to spare both the customer and the receipt any adventurous journeys. | Once is memorable enough. I now provide the paper with its own seat.

scene cleardesk
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sound desk edge makes a useful horizon when checking small drawings.
b : You line your ships up with the desk? | Which edge do you use?
a : Only on paper. The actual fleet is admirably free of my furniture. | The straight one nearest the window. The other has developed opinions about level.

scene helperroom
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.hand
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd leave a clear margin on any list I pass to #self.hand#.
b : For corrections? | Why not use the whole page?
a : Corrections and additions. Another reader may spot a valuable omission. | Because another writer deserves room to fit a point of view into the business.

scene spareprofit
when topic=prices self.likes=a_full_till
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy a full till chiefly because the empty one takes exactly as long to balance.
b : Would you admire the arithmetic either way? | You must save time on the empty one.
a : The arithmetic, perhaps. The prospect of dinner inclines me to prefer the first result. | It takes a surprising amount of hunting before you believe it's quite that empty.

scene fairprice
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't count an ornamental heading as three lines unless it actually takes that space.
b : Does a flourish cost extra? | Some customers want grand letters.
a : A small honest flourish comes with the letter. A whole landscape of ink would need discussing. | I'm happy to write them. I'd like us to know what the grandeur will cost beforehand.

scene bigstew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good mutton stew has an interesting lower storey beneath the broth.
b : What's filed down there? | Do you begin with the bottom?
a : Chunks of mutton, if the dish has been named with any sense of professional responsibility. | A sweep of the spoon from the bottom up is a fair sample of the whole affair.

scene smokesight
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke is an extremely inconsiderate editor of a skyline. | A few chimney puffs can remove a whole ship from a decent view.
b : Does it come back when the smoke clears? | Can you identify smoke by chimney?
a : The view comes back. Whether the vessel obliges is a separate question. | Sometimes. I would much rather identify the mast the chimney has chosen to revise.

scene ratcorner
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does warn / react.self / assess
a : I check the bottom edges of stored paper where a rat might take an interest.
b : Good nesting material? | How can you tell?
a : Exceptionally. I resent the unsolicited review of my stock by prospective tenants. | One ragged corner could be handling. A collection missing in neat bites suggests a reader with teeth.

scene stormroom
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder under a sound roof makes my desk seem part of a much larger room.
b : You enjoy the noise? | Doesn't it shake your writing?
a : Very much. The roof's presence is an important condition of my enthusiasm. | A loud peal is my signal to rest the pen. It usually finishes the sentence far more boldly than I intended.

scene rainstreak
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A streak of rain across the pane can add a mast to every roof in town.
b : You'd hardly mistake one. | What would identify the real mast?
a : Only for a blink. A blink is long enough to begin an unfortunate written certainty. | Move my head. The false mast moves sideways obediently over the entire fleet.

scene birdweather
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Birds arrive out of fog quite separately from the roofs beneath their feet.
b : Can you use them as markers then? | What does your page look like?
a : Only as evidence that some perch must exist. I wait for the masonry to introduce itself. | Several quite distinct birds and a most hypothetical city.

scene familybook
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd make a little finding book for #self.child# with one deliberate puzzle in the index.
b : Why a puzzle? | Would that make it less useful?
a : The pleasures of a private book differ from the solemn duties of a public list. | Slightly. I would accept that in exchange for an interesting conversation about the missing entry.

scene friendmargin
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could show #self.friend# an entry headed simply 'something with wings'.
b : An admission of defeat? | Would you put that in a public book?
a : An admirably accurate description of what I saw. A friend may appreciate its precision. | If the alternative was to invent a name, yes. I would prefer another look first.

scene officeview
when topic=home self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Office a good window offers an index of streets arranged by chimney height.
b : Is that how you find your own road? | Aren't they all black at the tops?
a : It would work from one particular window. On the ground I use the usual doorways. | The outlines are remarkably expressive. Some lean towards each other like two clerks sharing a remark.

scene halfpenny
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In lean times a customer may need one sound line of writing more than an entire decorated page.
b : Can you do much with one line? | Do you offer the single line?
a : A receipt will fit. So will an appointment correctly dated. Both useful little pieces. | Yes. I'd rather write something actually used than charge for a broad expanse of very costly air.

scene newstreet
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to test directions on a newcomer who never saw the vanished sign I was about to mention.
b : Gone a long time? | Can't a neighbour correct the directions?
a : Quite long enough to have become indispensable to those of us who remember it. | Not as well. A neighbour knows where I mean and might kindly pretend I told it clearly.

scene publicgossip
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A rumour with a memorable heading may outlive an excellent correction in smaller letters.
b : Would you give the correction a bigger heading? | Why repeat it then?
a : I might just set the whole rumour aside until something definite deserved lettering. | My thought exactly. I can generally find a more useful occupation for my ink.

scene rollingnews
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I treat an arrival seen from a window with slightly more confidence than an arrival described through one.
b : What if the sighting's poor? | You distrust witnesses?
a : Then it becomes a poor sighting with my name attached. Honest limits improve an account. | No. I distinguish my eyes from somebody else's. A simple but occasionally unpopular filing arrangement.

scene wagonin
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wagons in town mean there are papers in transit as well as goods.
b : What papers can you see? | Even blank paper could travel.
a : I can't say from a wheel mark. I merely allow space for a possible busy afternoon. | Yes. It's tremendously easy to write that particular consignment in advance without altering the goods.

scene latemule
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can write 'not yet arrived' in very small letters and still be perfectly understood.
b : What if the delay lengthens? | Why small letters?
a : Then I'll add a date. The original statement doesn't need a larger voice to remain accurate. | To leave room for actual news. A blank beginning needn't swallow the whole page.

scene quietcamp
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember a charcoal hill by its outline above a bare shoulder of trees.
b : Is that in your index too? | Wouldn't you rather remember the quiet?
a : In a private corner of it. A twig and a soft grey bank do duty for the whole view. | I do. A little line on a page can bring that remarkable hush back for a moment.

scene goodindex
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My ideal index lets a complete stranger find a ship without reading my mind.
b : Could a stranger use today's version? | What would have to change?
a : With assistance from three birds and a very patient clerk. There's room for improvement. | I'd remove the parts beginning 'as everybody knows'. They turn out to be quite numerous.

scene softchapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A chapel roof appears in more of my notes than any other fixed mark. | I'm grateful to have one quiet place that is also conspicuous enough to find.
b : Do you sit inside it often? | Does that make it a navigational blessing?
a : As often as I want the roofs to take a rest. Inside, there's no skyline to catalogue. | I should call it ordinary gratitude. Finding the door is generally the first part of making a visit.

scene festbanner
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Feast flags look marvellous in a view and miserable in permanent directions.
b : Couldn't you give the date? | Wouldn't a bright flag help today?
a : I do. The flags generally travel on to different poles without sending me an amendment. | Today, certainly. I'll politely ask tomorrow's walker to rely on the stone underneath.

scene blacknight
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At night a roof and a folded wing often become one dark notch. | My late notes are full of modest little qualifications.
b : Which is which? | How modest exactly?
a : If it takes off the question is resolved. Otherwise I put the pen away and hope for dawn. | Visible upright, possibly mast, probably wishful scribe. A very honest evening's work.

scene walkperspective
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Three steps along a street can lodge the same mast over a wholly different chimney.
b : Does your index mention where to stand? | That must be confusing.
a : With admirable emphasis. The observer is part of the observation whether flattered by it or not. | Only if one forgets the feet at the bottom of one's own point of view. I mark the corner.

grown

story roofguest [topic=memories|ships]
  : I once labelled a very small lateen shape at considerable distance. The angle of it was beautifully clear.
  : Shortly afterwards the entire sail flew to a different chimney and scratched its ear.
  b : What became of the identification?
  : A neat correction under birds. Fortunately I hadn't attempted to appoint its crew.

story inkwing [topic=work|memories self.role=merchant]
  : I wrote down a sharp little roof silhouette while quoting a fee to a customer. The marks ended up alongside each other.
  : For a moment my own account appeared to charge several coppers for a bird in flight.
  b : Did the customer notice?
  : I noticed, which was soon enough. I don't invoice wildlife without a very definite agreement.

story stewmast [topic=food|memories]
  : I sketched a view while a bowl of stew cooled on the sill. Looked down to find a mast I hadn't drawn.
  : A thin stem from the seasoning was leaning directly across my sketch.
  b : Did you include it in the final copy?
  : I included it in the washing up. My appetite for record keeping does have limits.

story countroof [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I counted seven birds along a ridge, turned a page and found eight. A moment later it was six.
  : The one count I could verify afterwards was the number of times I licked my pencil in irritation.
  b : How many times?
  : Twice too often, judging by the taste. The birds kept the rest of their account private.

story looseindex [topic=travel|memories]
  : I wrote my excellent directions on two slips of equal length and carried them in my sleeve. One slipped under the other.
  : Following them in the revised order returned me to my own front step in excellent time.
  b : Did you keep that route?
  : Certainly. I gave it a fresh heading. How to go nowhere with an air of great purpose.

rule @wing
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold the roofline fixed and let the feathers travel. | There's the mast beyond the second chimney.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A spelling confirmed now saves a scrape later. | Keep the copied page clear while the last line dries.

rule @bird
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four little heads on the cap. No, three and a bit of tile. | The rightmost bird has amended the index again.

rule @thund
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One excellent peal and only a very small ink blot. | That roof is earning its keep magnificently.

rule @nook
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give me the angle from beside the post, please. | A few steps and the whole fleet changes columns.

rule @count
when concept=bark self.likes=a_full_till
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The fee down plainly and the coin beside the entry. | A satisfying little sound from the till.

dlg resident.hub : I've space for a conversation provided it doesn't insist on fitting into one narrow column.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your entry continues on more than one page by now.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The roofs are rather less informative at night. A living visitor improves the view.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Ask from there, please. The papers aren't among the refreshments.
dlg resident.job [self.role=merchant self.job=scholar] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My preference is to sell one intelligible sentence than a very large mysterious paragraph.
dlg resident.job : My work ought to be understandable in my absence.
dlg resident.bye : May your chosen reference point continue to stand still.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=no] : A clear page where the gossip would belong. The empty space pleases me.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The report is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. My part is the reporting, which deserves a small separate heading.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : News has come by way of #world.news_from#. Here's the substance. #world.news#.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : We can look at what's wanted and establish the price before either paw strays towards the ink.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a repeat customer does possess one great advantage. You'll know what my flourishes cost.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : A fine display of bare counter today. I can still consider what you bring to sell.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : My pen is off duty. So is the paw generally attached to it.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Prices are quite legible from where you're standing. Point to what's wanted.
dlg shop.prices [here.shop=open] : Describe the work and I'll state the charge in ordinary numbers. Decorative figures cost extra.
dlg shop.bye : I hope whatever you take away is pleasantly easy to read.
dlg shop.bye [here.shop=asleep] : The pen and I are staying put till opening.

graft resident.hub
choice Could a bird help me locate a distant mast? -> wingmark
node wingmark
say See that chimney with a chipped corner? Find whichever bird happens to be there. Now shift your gaze half a chimney to the right. The mast is the fixed upright.
free
choice And if the bird leaves first? -> gonewing
choice I've found the upright. -> hub
node gonewing
say Use the chipped corner immediately. I employ the bird to make the view interesting. Only the brickwork has accepted a permanent appointment.
choice I'll rely on the brickwork. -> hub
choice I'll go try the view. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice How much space should I leave for an index? -> indexroom
node indexroom
say Save a small extra column for corrections or alternate names. The most useful directions often arrive after the elegant ones.
free
choice What if the column stays empty? -> whitespare
choice I'd like to look at the wares again. -> greet
node whitespare
say An empty column may indicate that all your entries were perfect. Leave the question open. Both perfection and a clear margin deserve a little room.
choice Back to the counter, please. -> greet
choice I'll leave space. Goodbye. -> bye
